# man — real-world examples

## Convert a man page to PDF

```sh
man -t bash | ps2pdf - bash.pdf
```

## View the ASCII chart

```sh
man 7 ascii
```

## Search man pages by keyword

```sh
man -k partition        # same as apropos
man -f printf           # same as whatis — one-line summary per section
```

## Read a page from a specific section

```sh
man 5 crontab     # file format, not the command
man 1 crontab     # the command
```

## Homelab: read a man page from a package that isn't installed locally

```sh
ssh david@homelab man zypper | less
```

## Homelab: grep straight through a page without opening it

```sh
man systemd.timer | grep -A2 'OnCalendar'
```

## Homelab: page man in your preferred pager with color

```sh
MANPAGER="less -R" man rsync
```

| Flag / section | What it does                     |
| -------------- | -------------------------------- |
| -k <word>      | keyword search (apropos)         |
| -f <cmd>       | one-line description (whatis)    |
| -t             | typeset (PostScript) output      |
| 1              | user commands                    |
| 5              | file formats                     |
| 7              | misc (ascii, signal, ...)        |
| 8              | admin commands                   |
